      "widgets_values": [
        "### Global Metadata\nA creative 30-second Chinese guochao hip-hop anthem at 112 BPM in 4/4. Fuse thunderous Chinese Dagu, piercing Suona, Pipa, Guzheng, Erhu, gongs, cymbals, modern hip-hop drums, and powerful sub-bass. Fiery, heroic, youthful, and cinematic, with the image of an ancient red dragon awakening in a modern city. End sharply at exactly 30 seconds.\n\n### Vocal Details\nA commanding male Mandarin rapper with a deep, powerful chest voice. Use a brisk, punchy flow with crisp consonants, strong rhythmic accents, and continuous forward momentum. Deliver the Chorus like a forceful rhythmic proclamation without slowing down. Start rapping on the first downbeat. No laughter, chuckles, spoken ad-libs, vocal improvisation, or prolonged melisma.\n\n### Arrangement\nBegin with the first lyric and a synchronized Dagu strike; no instrumental intro. Keep heavy drums and sub-bass moving continuously beneath the vocal. Use short ascending Suona strikes only in the gaps between lines, while Pipa and Guzheng add sharp rhythmic attacks. Expand into the full Chinese ensemble at the Chorus without changing tempo. No instrumental interlude, solo, repeated section, second Chorus, or fade-out. After the final word, play one compact Dagu-and-Suona closing cadence, then cut all sound sharply at exactly 30.0 seconds.",
        "[Verse]\n大鼓落，惊雷撞城墙  \n唢呐起，赤龙破穹苍  \n黄河在低音里翻滚发烫  \n我踩五千年的鼓点登场  \n\n[Chorus]\n墨作浪，笔作枪  \n一撇一捺撑起东方  \n让世界听见山河回响  \n这就是华夏少年的锋芒",
        222,
        "fixed",
        30,
        1.5,
        60
      ],
      "color": "#aecf2a",
      "bgcolor": "#393e25"
    },
